        "explanation": "<h3>Comparing Quantities</h3><p>A <strong>Ratio</strong> compares two values. It shows how much of one thing there is compared to another.</p><p>Format: <strong>a : b</strong> (Read as 'a to b').</p><p>Example: If there are 2 apples and 3 oranges, the ratio of apples to oranges is <strong>2:3</strong>.</p><div class='interactive-block'><h4>Try It!</h4><p>If you have 1 red pen and 2 blue pens, what is the ratio of red to blue? (Format: x:y)</p><input type='text' class='form-control' placeholder='e.g. 1:1'><button class='btn btn-sm btn-primary try-it-btn' data-answer='1:2'>Check</button><div class='feedback'></div></div>",
